data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":799,"item_id":"msg_0bbd46bcfd62a65e016b0a01ca0d3c87d18808414287a2072a","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"bram\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"reuse\\\",\\\"ability\\\":\\\"unheated-food-preparation\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Its inspect operation already examines owned food, records visible condition and treatment, and explicitly leaves safety unknown. Inspection does not require preparing or consuming a whole unit, so it applies to the held 1.9-unit berry stack. This supplies the requested feasible, non-ingestive assessment with explicit limits; a new safety-test capability would duplicate that function or imply unsupported diagnostic power. Probe and the thermal and mechanical inspection capabilities likewise do not establish chemical safety.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Reuse unheated-food-preparation's existing inspect operation, not prepare. After individual learning, invoke mode inspect with inputStackId item-212-bram-2914. The general operation accepts an applicable actor's own food stack, rather than being bound to Bram or berries. Prerequisites: the referenced food must still be owned and available for inspection, and the actor must have the required energy. Cost: one execution round and 0.2 energy; no food, water, tool, vessel, fuel or other material is consumed, supplied, reserved or moved. The separate prepare operation's whole-unit restriction and 0.5-energy preparation cost do not apply to inspect. Execute the existing contract and handler; record implementation reuse, not reinvention. Produce an observable inspection event and an unverified personal record of the represented visible condition, treatment and any existing personal eating record. Do not expose hidden nutrition, toxicity or source stock. Distinguish observations from established food knowledge: the verified berry press record berry:load response:load-band-0, supported by event-213-bram-2933, establishes only its stated mechanical response; item-212-bram-2914:observed-state, supported by event-217-bram-2983, is an unverified visible-state record, not an edibility test. Bram's hazelnut knowledge does not establish anything about berries and supplies no hazelnuts. For these berries the warranted conclusion is safety undetermined, not safe or toxic. Visible spoilage, if actually represented and observed, can support reporting unsuitable condition, but absence of visible spoilage cannot establish safety. No tasting, pressing, heating, detoxification, nutrition change or feeding occurs. Preserve stack quantity, origin, age and ongoing decay; ordinary world processes continue only during actual learning and action rounds. Inspection is one complete round, with no staged preparation progress or background process. An interrupted, cancelled or death-terminated incomplete inspection must not create a completed assessment or success event; retain only actually completed effects and charges under the existing execution rules, without duplicating charges, outputs or refunds. A later attempt is a new paid inspection, not free resumed work. There is no maintenance, reserved material to return, material refund or ongoing safety guarantee. Development/review waiting itself advances no time.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Reuse the existing two-round individual study requirement; availability is not mastery. The existing capability grants no reward, and learning, requesting, inspecting a record or repeating an unchanged inspection must not manufacture pleasure or satisfaction. A genuinely informative observation or informative inability to determine safety can be recorded as evidence, but this reuse adds no experience-award mechanism. No consumption, nutrition, comfort or mood effect occurs, and no protected reward account, budget, goal or permission changes.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit or reuse inspection visuals only for an actually performed examination. Reuse the existing food appearance and attach reusable event metadata identifying actor, target stack, operation inspect, completion state, observed condition, evidence reference and uncertainty status. Represent safety as unknown rather than showing a safe-food badge, toxin-free glow, cooked state or successful preparation. Rejected or interrupted attempts may show their actual incomplete status but cannot display a completed assessment; no food transformation or new physical product is depicted.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

